            <h2 class="language-text">en</h2>
            <p><span class="bold-text">Ítalo Carajá</span> (Belo Horizonte/MG, 2000) is a visual artist. He holds a degree in Visual Arts from the Federal University of Minas Gerais (EBA/UFMG) and lives and works in Belo Horizonte, MG.</p>

            <p>His practice spans drawing, painting, and installation, often working with found objects and printed matter. He investigates how images and meanings are constructed through everyday materials, with a focus on memory, repetition, and the circulation of visual culture. His recent work explores the relationships between play, mediation, and violence, examining how these dynamics are absorbed and reproduced through banal objects and systems of representation.</p>

